{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1493650-tc-2e-tech-in-various-eras","id":1493650,"title":"[TC 2E] Tech in various Eras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-24T16:37:14-07:00","id":1493650,"title":"[TC 2E] Tech in various Eras","content":"So as Trinity Eras reflects various variants of SF - so does Technology in it. Here is general sum up - correctly me if I'm wrong...<br /> <br /> <b>Aether</b> 1890s - Tech older than the era itself is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-%F0%9F%98%B2\">called Magic or Alchemy</a>...<br /> <br /> <b>Adventure</b> 1920-30s - Inspired Science can make anything you want. Few Mesmerists are described as using Magic by their uneducated peers.<br /> <br /> <b>Core / Assassins</b> 2020s - Our real world modern Tech - with a bit dosage of Super Science, like from James Bond <i><b>007</b></i> movies.<br /> <br /> <b>Aberrant</b> 2020-30s - Super Science of Nova is changing the world. Think here about many <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solarpunk\" target=\"_blank\">Solarpunk</a> projects we describe in popculture.<br /> <br /> <b>Anima </b>2080s - Cyberpunk true era! World is rebuilding after Aberrant Wars in 2050-60s and it's effect - literal <b><i>Crash</i></b> of Aberrant era wonders, Internet as we know it also. In FSA started <i><b>Cascade City</b></i> project, where government gives <i>GLASS</i> head implants to citizens for free - but ending on addicting them, spy of them and showing other concerning topics about technology. In 2086 the UN passes the <b>Shanghai Accords</b>, a treaty that bans computer enhancement and technologies that allows electronic access to thoughts and memories such as GLASS, as well as placing severe restrictions on the usage of true Artificial Intelligence in anything but controlled environments.<br /> <br /> <b>Aeon</b> 2120s - <b>Star Trek</b>-like era? By Shanghai Accords, implants and cyberwere are illegal. You only use something like hologlasses or smart eye lances, that they can put out in any moment they do not like it? So all have basically personal computer - like with GLASS in <b>Anima</b> - only <u>not implanted in body</u> or brain, but just <b><i>outside devices</i></b>?<br /> <br /> <b>Next^x version of </b><b>Microsoft HoloLens 2?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/k_eNxzn9DT0?t=41\" data-code=\"k_eNxzn9DT0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/k_eNxzn9DT0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-24-2022, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T06:30:13-07:00","id":1493668,"title":"","content":"I'd say <b>Core</b> is actually still close to <b>Adventure!</b> supertech-wise, it's just not as common. Or rather there's still roughly the same number of Talents going around making the occasional device, but they're a smaller portion of the population.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue that <b>Aeon</b> isn't at the Star Trek level, rather the high end of cyberpunk. Thematically it's much more post-cyberpunk than Anima is, even in the FSA, but they haven't quite broken through to proper post-scarcity levels. Humans aren't yet obsolete, but there's clear signs that massive changes to the species are coming. Particularly if they can reverse engineer those Prometheus Chambers. Revelation Space might be a good ballpark for the upper end of non-psi Aeon capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T08:19:09-07:00","id":1493729,"title":"","content":"I think it's better if you imagine Aeon as a biopunk setting, with a few exceptions like Nippon. Biotechnology has, for the most part, overtaken hardtech since it's much more &quot;natural&quot; and easy to implant on the human body. However, this technology is not equally distributed or universally accepted, which is one of the main factors, alongside geopolitical divides, that prevents a post-scarcity society. <br /> Cyberware is not illegal, only brain implants or anything that can mess with your mind or control you, so yes, only outside devices (I assume you can have artificial eyes that allow you to see in augmented reality). In any case, the majority of people has abandoned cyberware, advances in biotechnology has made them mostly redundant, there are few cybernetic implants that can't be reproduced via biotech. <br /> If I remember correctly, the developers talked about a possible new era in the future heavily influenced by Space Opera, I believe it would be more common to see Star Trek technology level there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}